  str_loading_e_h_name80050003 = "Millennia-Old Faith",
  str_loading_e_h_name80050004 = "Millennia-Old Rivalry",
  str_loading_desc1 = "Under Lumopolis, the land of vast shadows, countless people who live on trading and information exchange form huge towns, while various underground forces are the de facto rulers of these places.",
  str_loading_desc2 = "The region known as Astra is the pearl in the twilight circle, and for plenty of Aurorians, it is the only place known as home, where there is a regular alternation of day and night for life to flourish.",
  str_loading_desc3 = "Located in the cold north, the people can live here in peace, thanks to the powerful magic power guarding this small area. Important matters are decided by Queen Bethlehem.",
  str_loading_desc4 = "The last Darkover Crisis started seventeen years ago and was quelled by an alliance of numerous factions. However, even in close-knitted communities exist disputes and animosity. Especially the Aurorians...",
  str_loading_desc5 = "The only known habitat of the Eclipsites. Some say it has something to do with the various fragments left behind by the ancient civilization. We can only speculate that it might be the instinct of Eclipsites to inhabit here, or it might be the work of the mysterious organization, Eclipse...",
  str_loading_desc6 = "It's an abyss where no light shines, where the architecture is strange and treacherous, and the wondrous craftsmanship of the ancients can always be found. Numerous adventurers came to this place like moths to a flame for the relics and trophies from an unknown era, just to be buried here...",
  str_loading_desc7 = "After the Darkover Crisis involving massive attacks by the Eclipsites 17 years ago, a few Caelestites managed to escape Eraveil. Soroz also took a Caelestite and hid underground, isolated from the world.",
  str_loading_desc8 = "Many years ago, when Eclipsites were running rampant, this thousands of meters deep underground city saved countless lives. The people of Gannon City organized efficiently and developed the unique Lumina technology to build its defense system centered around Gannon City.",
  str_loading_desc9 = "Aurorians, Eclipsites, Illumina, Lumopolis... There is too much information in your head. Does the reassembly of Eclipsites have anything to do with the Darkover Crisis that happened seventeen years ago? The truth-seeking journey is destined to be full of ups and downs...",
  str_loading_desc10 = "A disorderly and outspoken nomadic alliance formed by nomadic wanderers. Its hardy members smell of the road and the wind, wandering around the Rediesel Desert, living an unfettered, carefree life.",
  str_loading_desc11 = "Supposedly the organization masterminded the Darkover Crisis; which true motive is unknown to anyone. It is composed of high-level Eclipsites and has absorbed many rebels from other races for an unknown purpose. The Eclipse disappeared without a trace after the coalition forces of city-states in the Astra region dealt with the Darkover Crisis...",
  str_loading_desc12 = "Built on a floating island called \"Azurite\", this city is the safest stronghold in the world. It currently has a distinctive power hierarchy, with a triumvirate of the Governor, the Elder Council from the Noble, and the Priests of the Temple. The nobles of Lumopolis are dedicated to maintaining the current order, while the Temple promotes the worship of the sun.",
  str_loading_desc13 = "A loose federation of a large number of settlements centered around a huge undercity called Gannon, located on the front lines of the battle against the Eclipsites. The Illumina Federation has adopted a collective leadership system, establishing a completely different form of society from that of Lumopolis.",
  str_loading_desc14 = "Colossus, a legacy from the ancient civilization. It has so many secrets that it is said to be impossible to analyze its structure and understand the principles behind it, not even with all the current knowledge and every scholar's effort combined. A lot of them can't even be maneuvered directly; only the Caelestites can link to the Colossus' intelligence with their psychic ability to form a deep level of control and operate it from there.",
  str_loading_desc15 = "The chaos caused by the Darkover Crisis 17 years ago led to the loss of several mysterious objects of Caelestites. No one knows their whereabouts. Even their true purpose has been deliberately hidden...",
  str_loading_desc16 = "Shadowlord, or Istvan, is the most feared in Umbraton. It's said that his personal museum of collections, the Whispering Corridor, contains a large number of horrifying collectibles. If you're lucky enough to survive the dangers hidden behind the bricks and cobwebs, you may find interesting things here...",
  str_loading_desc17 = "The residents of Umbraton seem to have two sides: smiling and cold, kind and harsh. This is also a characteristic of Umbraton. As long as you adapt to it, this place is heaven, and if not, it will be hell.",
  str_loading_desc18 = "In the continent of Astra, traces of countless relics from ancient times have been revealed, and the newly discovered Spire is one of them. What astonishes people about it is not only its height, but also its amazing power, and the legends about hidden treasures inside...",
  str_loading_desc19 = "Those who gain their power from Light and fight with it are the main inhabitants of this continent. Apart from them, few groups can confront the Eclipsites head-on.",
  str_loading_desc20 = "Creatures of unknown origin. They have been the mortal enemies of all communities since the beginning of recorded history. Except for the Aurorians, almost no one can fight against them.",
  str_loading_desc21 = "Material for making a help signal. Can be used to recruit Aurorians to join the adventure. Unfortunately, there is no guarantee about who will respond to such a signal.",
  str_loading_desc22 = "It looks like a piano, and commands are input by playing on this Colossus control panel. Only Caelestites can understand its language well.",
  str_loading_desc23 = [[
Natural barriers and numerous Colossi secured peace here for hundreds of years.
Just like the Colossi technologies, the origin of the Caelestites is shrouded in mystery and is impossible to verify.
If this peace can last forever, this place will once again flourish as it did before.]],
  str_loading_desc24 = [[
Time has not healed the scars of seventeen years ago. What happened that day lives on in the vivid reality of the present.
Since that day, no one has returned to this place... until today.]],
  str_loading_desc25 = [[
That day coincided with a major festival, and the people were unprepared.
The fall of Eraveil seems to have been inevitable, and Schummer was merely a necessary catalyst.]],
  str_loading_desc26 = [[
Aviduz was once a special unit among the many Colossi of Eraveil.
Huge in size, and unparalleled in function, it possessed unlimited potential.
Because of this, the demands placed on its Navigator were also particularly stringent.]],
  str_loading_desc27 = [[
At Aviduz's core lies a healing pod that can provide emergency treatment to the gravely injured.
Under the providence of some mysterious force, Schummer recovered far greater power than anyone expected.]],
  str_loading_desc28 = [[
A dark area located at the edge of Eternal Night. Here, the days are short and the nights are long, and the entire place brims with Darkflow.
There used to be many Aurorian settlements here, but they've all been abandoned for quite some time now. Dilapidated ruins continue to crumble, and the bustling liveliness of the past lies covered in dust.
Today, all that's left are wastelands, ruins, and swarms of Eclipsites, and no sane Aurorian is willing to set foot here again due to the lingering Darkflow...]],
  str_loading_desc29 = [[
An Undercity located on the edge of Eternal Night that once served as the Illumina Federation's foothold against the Eclipsites.
However, after a long ago Eclipsite invasion, it was abandoned.
There's said to be loads of supplies and technologies left behind from when Illumina's soldiers retreated, but few are willing to brave the dense Darkflow and face the Eclipsite army to retrieve them.]],
  str_loading_desc30 = [[
There aren't many who know about this old escape tunnel, but it's a miracle that it still exists to this day.
It may be the only way to the surface, so it's best to follow it.
Defeat every enemy you come across in this ancient, bullet-strewn passageway. You might just escape, and who knows, it may lead you to the final battle.]],
  str_loading_h_desc1 = [[
This is the Rediesel Desert of Southern Astra, where an endless sea of golden sand stretches as far as the eye can see.
Under the gaze of the blazing sun, this barren, drought-ridden land is one of the most uninhabitable places in Astra.
Only the most stubborn and tenacious forms of life can find freedom here.]],
  str_loading_h_desc2 = [[
Only by passing through bitter winds and unrelenting rain can one reach the eye of the storm of the Red-Eye Gorge.
The volcanic ash that once ravaged the land now acts as a fertilizer, filling this verdant expanse with life.
It is almost as if the tragedy of long ago never even took place...]],
  str_loading_h_desc3 = [[
The atmosphere of this concrete underground laboratory is intrinsically dull and depressing.
Surgical tools are strewn across open worktops, their cold, heartless contours reflecting a menacing flash of light.
But it is only from such a place that the most beautiful flowers blossom.]],
  str_loading_h_desc4 = [[
In Eve's memory, the skies of her hometown were a cloudless, bright blue.
If things hadn't changed so suddenly, maybe that fleeting moment of happiness could have lasted forever.
But just maybe...]],
  str_loading_h_desc5 = [[
In an oasis deep in the Rediesel Desert, there exists a street built by the Rediesel Wrench.
Although the street looks run-down, every dilapidated brick is filled with love.
This humble stretch of land is the most tender place in the world.]],
  str_loading_h_desc6 = [[
The Tir' Hotel is the premier holiday destination of the Lumopolis nobility.
It's simply the best place to enjoy the beautiful scenery of the Celestial Coast!
Reservations are currently available at a limited-time discount.]],
  str_loading_h_desc7 = [[
The Ocean Sovereign is a sacrificial ceremony originating from the Aurorians who once lived on this coast.
The participants must accept various trials and complete difficult challenges.
It is believed that their triumph will bring blessings of good weather and an abundance of fish.]],
  str_loading_h_desc8 = [[
An ancient legend tells of a castle that emerged from the sea.
In order to save his people, a monarch accepted the trials of the goddesses.
Time has flowed onward, the crisis has long since passed, yet the Monarch has not returned.]],
  str_loading_h_desc9 = [[
It is not clear who willed this domain into existence, but it is a void filled with strange visions.
Within it lie those who blindly seek the power of the lost brave, and those who long for the opportunity to escape their bondage.
Embrace your curse and break down its walls.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10 = [[
Facing defeat, Caroline cursed everyone with the last of her strength.
And the Monarch she longed to resurrect just may have heard her plea...]],
  str_loading_h_desc11 = [[
It's time for the scroungers to move again.
These shady thieves emerge from the darkness, only to return to the shadows as quickly as they appeared.]],
  str_loading_h_desc12 = "On the barren desert wasteland is an Illumina Undercity watchtower. It has been here since Illumina established this Undercity and the Defensive Line, witnessing the tireless struggles of Illumina's unyielding soldiers.",
  str_loading_h_desc13 = "This is the battlefield on the Undercity's outskirts. The soldiers of Illumina have erected fortifications here said to be capable of stopping the advances of most Eclipsite attackers.",
  str_loading_h_desc14 = "This transport station stands at the gates of Undercity 24, and is where goods coming in and out of the city are handled. Even though no one works here now, from the hoisting towers, transport vehicles, and wide array of goods, you can see that the people here live an active and well-ordered life.",
  str_loading_h_desc15 = "An abandoned Illumina Undercity, devastated by a huge fire. The civilians who once lived here were evacuated, and the soldiers who lived here now fight on the front line. Each former inhabitant battles on to carry out their own duty, determined to return to their home one day.",
  str_loading_h_desc16 = "In Illumina, even the passages possess a radiant lucidity, shining with the light of steel. Upon seeing this passage for the first time, one cannot help but comment on how bright it is.",
  str_loading_h_desc17 = [[
During this festival, the Caelestites practiced all kinds of interesting customs and decorated their homes.
They believed that they could connect with nature and their ancestors through these customs.]],
  str_loading_h_desc18 = [[
History is like a feather, trapped beneath a heavy shell.
The path to the future depends on how we navigate the road ahead.]],
  str_loading_h_desc19 = "Free trade in a free market—anything can be traded in Umbraton.\nGuilds are the embodiment of commerce and capital, bringing boundless vitality to Umbraton.",
  str_loading_h_desc20 = "The underground gangs of Umbraton are known as \"shadows in the shadow.\" Operating within the gray area, they cannot afford to expose themselves to the public eye. However, they dream of using their furtive subversion to become an overnight success, accepted in broader society. When dark clouds form overhead, they begin to put all manner of secret operations in motion...",
  str_loading_h_desc21 = "The Dam of Scars stands tall and proud through natural or manufactured disasters, rainstorms or warfare. Not only has it proven its tenacity to its builder, the Shadowlord, it has also brought a great sense of security to the people of Umbraton.",
  str_loading_h_desc22 = "The nobles of Lumopolis parade their wealth with pride, though their sumptuous display of luxury is born from the hard work of the common masses who dwell in the city below Lumopolis. Although it is a world apart from the manors of the nobility, life flows onward with a warm and resolute vitality. After all, this is still a part of Lumopolis. Even with lower status, people are much better off than those who live outside the confines of the city.",
  str_loading_h_desc23 = "As the center of Aurorian civilization, Lumopolis considers itself the leader of the continent's forces. For this reason, this hall was built to show the strength and glory of Lumopolis to the foreign leaders invited to the city to participate in meetings of global significance. In this way, Lumopolis maintains the upper hand in all conferences attended by these various forces and makes a myriad of decisions that influence the entire continent according to its ideals.",
  str_loading_h_desc24 = "Festival fireworks envelop the entirety of the Azurite. Under a brilliant display, people gather together to enjoy a grand celebration. As the center of civilization in Astra, Lumopolis deserves such a day. But every day must come to an end.",
  str_loading_h_desc25 = "For the people of Northland, the land of perennial winter, a snowcapped forest is a familiar sight. When the first light of dawn shines on these frozen treetops, the sun's rays refract through their countless icicles, composing an infinite concerto of innumerable dazzling beams that have now come to symbolize the faith of all who call this land home.",
  str_loading_h_desc26 = "Many people claim that this lake was created by a glacier that melted long ago, but none can explain why this deep, tranquil, and mirror-like lake remains unfrozen all year round. This is why many people believe that the appearance of Lake Mirror was a gift from the heavens. It is rumored that when the Northland royal family once visited this place, they saw a vision, and the narcissus flowers that bloom around Lake Mirror further add to its mystery.",
  str_loading_h_desc27 = "Some say that the first dawn that breaks on Northland's horizon is what protects this place, dispelling the invasion of darkness from the land of eternal night. However, other legends claim that the true power of Northland lies in an undying resolve to protect this land—a resolve brighter than the resplendent Aurora and the radiant dawn, forever unchanging and eternally glorious.",
  str_loading_h_desc28 = [[
Entire ruins, completely isolated from the world and filled with buildings that have never been seen before.
There seems to be no trace of the original inhabitants.]],
  str_loading_h_desc29 = [[
For unknown reasons, the ruins are quickly collapsing.
Both the machines that are busily repairing the ruins and the Eclipsites living within have become volatile.]],
  str_loading_h_desc30 = [[
There are still many unsolved secrets in this city.
Unless everyone already has an answer in their hearts...]],
  str_loading_h_desc31 = "This energy core has been running for years beyond measure. It's struggling like a dying patient. Every heartbeat could well be the last.",
  str_loading_h_desc32 = "Abby's data hub. This mad biological module is constantly producing and enhancing Eclipsites. Their irascible and horrific screams have haunted the hub.",
  str_loading_h_desc33 = "A small island east of Astra that's rich in resources and has relatively few Eclipsites. A century ago, Koufu-jou was built in the center of Cloud Island and a general was sent by the main island to govern the place. Since then, the two islands have been at odds with each other. Behind a past feared by Cloud Island natives, this general is about to take his secrets and Cloud Island into an unforeseeable future...",
  str_loading_h_desc34 = "Cloud Island's traditional Kasuga Festival has been preserved through the tides of time. Times change, and people live and die, but the cherry blossoms will always be the same.",
  str_loading_h_desc35 = "The Night Festivities is a special event that is held in Koufu-jou in memory of the spirits of those who have passed. Every year when the cherry trees bloom, people host the Kasuga Festival. At night, everyone gathers to march down the streets, wearing cat masks and carrying lanterns. They believe that during this march, they can connect with the afterlife and see their loved ones one more time.",
  str_loading_h_desc36 = "Koufu-jou is located at the highest point of Cloud Island, looking down on it from behind a veil of clouds and mystery. It was built brick upon brick in the distant past, but when the raging fire consumed it all, people were forced to reflect on what they wanted of the future. How many had cheered for war, and how many had perished in the blazing flames...",
  str_loading_h_desc37 = "During the hours of Yin, restless souls take on physical shapes, creating a force field that haunts Cloud Island. During the hours of Yang, a divine artifact takes shape that possesses the power to eliminate all evil spirits. However, when both Yin and Yang are in the hands of a greedy and selfish person, their unbridled desires are transformed into something much more terrifying than ghosts.",
  str_loading_h_desc38 = "Located in the southern part of the Rediesel Desert, relentless gales blanket its surroundings in a searing yellow haze as far as the eye can see, punctuated only by white bones and dead trees with no hint of greenery in sight. But even in this grim and desolate place, there are still signs of life. Besides the flare scorpions and crimson ring snakes hiding in the shadows of the rocks, there are even bigger predators lurking in the sea of sand. This is a place where the weak are swallowed whole.",
  str_loading_h_desc39 = "The land around the volcano is littered with black rough sandstone. Seen from atop, blazing lava flows down the mountain's fissures, forming a spectacular lava waterfall at the edge of a ravine. The closer one gets to the volcano, the hotter the air becomes, making breathing difficult. What's even more amazing is the smaller pieces of sandstone floating in the air due to mysterious forces.",
  str_loading_h_desc40 = "Blazing Tooth Canyon, near the edge of Eternal Night, gets its name from its jagged landscape. Its steep sides seem to plunge into the ground where a river, long dried up under the scorching sun, winds around and is covered in so many cracks that it can hardly be called a road. But perhaps it's because these features act as such insurmountable obstacles that it was designated as the location for Rediesel Wrench's first rally track...",
  str_loading_h_desc41 = "To conceal a room, cover the gate with bricks and tiles and fill the windows with sand and mud. Turn it into part of an insignificant street or wall and wipe it off the map forever. A corner of this world is gone but nobody knows. It's reserved exclusively for the True Order. Lumopolis is very big, where a hole like this passes easily unnoticed.",
  str_loading_h_desc42 = "Standing behind the thick curtain before the show starts, you must contain your pounding heart for this stage allows no one to stop once the curtain is drawn open. The answer to a perfect performance lies only in your next attempt.",
  str_loading_h_desc43 = "It's safe to say that puppets are devoid of life and soul. But when it strikes a living pose, it might make one think it's more human than the living themselves. Perhaps it's because we fantasize that objects like that have souls.",
  str_loading_h_desc44 = "If there's one thing that represents Eraveil, it'd be the dandelion. These fluffy little white flowers grow throughout Eraveil, and a gust of wind is all it takes to create the illusion of falling snow. Some don't like dandelions because they feel that they lack fidelity, always taking root where the wind leads them. But in Eraveil, you'll find that no matter which direction the wind blows, one can always see large groups of dandelions suspended in the air. They come and go with the wind, but they have always remained.",
  str_loading_h_desc45 = "Eraveil is a serene place where gentle winds blow over endless plains of green, and the air is always refreshing. Despite that, the sight grows tiring and evokes an emptiness that can be felt deep down, as if something is missing. Where are the roosters calling at the crack of dawn, and the smoke rising from chimneys in the evenings?",
  str_loading_h_desc46 = [[
Following the guide, you return to Eraveil, a place with many familiar memories.
Beneath Eraveil, however, lies a secret.
This secret is about Eraveil, the past and the future, and about you.]],
  str_loading_h_desc47 = [[
Hidden in the vast space beneath the White Tower is an entrance that leads underground!
You may well be the first to unlock it again after thousands of years.
Explore the deep underground ruins... And there, you might find what you've been looking for.]],
  str_loading_h_desc48 = [[
The mysterious ring-shaped device at the center of the "Colossus Maintenance Base" beneath Eraveil seems to be the control center of the entire base that kept the vast complex running all this while.
However, it doesn't look like it's been maintained for a long time and I'm not sure if it still works...]],
  str_loading_h_desc49 = [[
The existence of the white tower in Eraveil is a secret in itself.
The soaring White Tower resonates with ancient technologies that still exist today. Does this resonance represent a threat from the past, or hope for the future?]],
  str_loading_h_desc50 = "The mysterious device in Eraveil's underground base appears to have the power to transform Aurorians. Knowledge of how it works is lost, and no one knows what it can actually do. To use it, one must consider the risks involved...",
  str_loading_h_desc51 = [[
You came back here to use the "Chord of the Law."
Though this path may prove too difficult for a Caelestite, even the tiniest bit of hope is worth holding on to.]],
  str_loading_h_desc52 = "Harmonious atmosphere and natural scenery... To a Caelestite, there is no better heritage than Cloud Gardens. There is much to do in this land of white towers. Every insignificant existence in your hands will become part of the future that belongs to the Caelestite.",
  str_loading_h_desc53 = "The Fountain of Hope in front of the Hyacinth Tower is the heart of Cloud Gardens. You can chat with your friends, release the fish you've caught in the pond, or throw a sparkling Hope Coin into the pond to make a shimmering wish.",
  str_loading_h_desc54 = "The most common room in Cloud Gardens. It has good lighting and excellent ventilation, making it a perfect living or storage space. However, remember to clean it well before using it.",
  str_loading_h_desc55 = "Under the well-laid quilt are dirty clothes that haven't been washed in a week. The tightly-packed cabinet is filled with cups that are about to fall. Half-eaten Crunchy Munchy Crunches, books, and magazines are scattered all over the place... Isn't this normal for a boy's room?",
  str_loading_h_desc56 = "\"There's no everlasting family, but only profit.\" Like many old-fashioned families in Umbraton, every brick and tile of the Andersen family's home was built out of huge profits. The current Count Andersen, however, seems to have different investment preferences.",
  str_loading_h_desc57 = "Make your family's guests feel at home and inspire fear in your family's enemies. The master's order must be carried out no matter what. However, the butler and the master's personalities are equal—the elite butler of the Andersen family is perfect and shows no mercy even when he is testing his master.",
  str_loading_h_desc58 = [[
Wondrous beasts are usually found away from people, living freely in the mountains, forests, wilderness, snowfields, or deep ocean. Unlike normal animals, they can use Lumina and have various unique abilities or characteristics. These friendly creatures rarely interact with Aurorians, but they often lend a helping hand in the face of a crisis.
At the same time, however, changes in their habitats and their own reproductive deficiencies have led to a decline in their overall population, and many wondrous beasts are now endangered.]],
  str_loading_h_desc59 = [[
Where wondrous beasts appear, you will also find the extrozoologists nearby. Although they are far rarer than wondrous beasts, they're incredibly passionate about their work. They follow trails of wondrous beasts to the ends of the world, keep record of their ecology and characteristics, and compile these records into books as their legacy. They also aid the wondrous beasts when they are in danger.
Fia is on her way to becoming an extrozoologist through her own earnest efforts.]],
  str_loading_h_desc60 = "The whereabouts of The Illusionist & Old Bill's Circus have always been unknown. Recently, there are words that they have been invited to the famous port city, Harbor City. The ringmaster, Jeno, is an eccentric person, and his subordinates all have unique skills. He wants to give the local citizens a great summer festival to remember.",
  str_loading_h_desc61 = "The city lord of Harbor City seems quite obsessed with the Emerald. What could be there? What secrets are hiding? The hustle and bustle of the celebration will soon subside, and the dormant undercurrent under the deck will soon surge...",
  str_loading_h_desc62 = "The chaos created by Elvis seems to have come to an end after his arrest, but no one actually knows why he did all this. The doubts in Carleen's heart made her as gloomy as the weather in Harbor City. When will the truth come to light? To get to the bottom of this, Carleen and her party have stayed in Harbor City to conduct investigations. Meanwhile, it seems Elvis still hasn't decided on his plan.",
  str_loading_h_desc63 = "The ancient seal has been shaken, awakening the legendary Eclipsite sleeping under the deep sea. A war at the coastline is about to break out as the waves sweep towards Harbor City. In the face of imminent battle with Eclipsites, will the party be able to protect Harbor City? Will Elvis find a solution to this crisis?",
  str_loading_h_desc64 = "The Cloudwhale dispelled the Darkflow permeating through the air and cut through the dark clouds shrouding Harbor City. By the time the sun shined on Harbor City, it seemed that everything had taken a turn for the better, and even the howling wind seemed to be showing signs of stopping.",
  str_loading_h_desc65 = [[
The Eclipsites invaded 12 years ago.
After countless hellish battles, this is what was left of Euphoria.
Wounds that never healed, gradually festering.]],
  str_loading_h_desc66 = [[
This town is saddled with too many sins from the past.
They grow like tumors on a body, and must be removed to recover.
Perhaps only then will sunshine return to this place.]],
  str_loading_h_desc67 = "—This is how it was advertised in the newspaper. This building on the outskirts of Umbraton has had countless owners over the years. Only recently did it come into the possession of the Andersens, who made it the haunted house it is today. It was supposedly built by an eccentric architect who was the mastermind behind the designing of the false stairwell, misplaced doors, and windows. All the bizarre chandeliers and paintings were of his own design.",
  str_loading_h_desc68 = "A peculiar basement rests beneath what is now known as the Andersen Haunted House. I know you've never seen it for yourself. It's possible that even the current owner has never laid eyes on it. The last owner of the house set foot in there just once and sold the place shortly afterward before moving far, far away. There are plenty of rumors surrounding the basement, but I don't believe a single one. After all, the living have no way of knowing the truth.",
  str_loading_h_desc69 = [[
The Illumina Research Center is the science and technology hub of the Illumina Federation.
The researchers here are responsible for analyzing ancient technological devices and innovating new technologies.
However, there is no end to research. Will you find the information you seek here?]],
  str_loading_h_desc70 = [[
The battlefield simulator made by the Illumina Research Center can bring you to any battle recorded in its system.
Do not question the authenticity of the scenes it conjures for you: the desperate soldiers, ferocious Eclipsites, the sun eclipsed by the flames of war.... Everything you see here actually happened.]],
  str_loading_h_desc71 = "Numbers and science are incomprehensible and distant. The strange thing is that they might just abruptly present emotions and intentions in an incomparably precise way in front of us. Some distances are actually even more frightening once they can be measured.",
  str_loading_h_desc72 = "A place where Lumopolis' sun doesn't shine, outside the defense line of Illumina's Undercities. This town is the last place where Aurorians gather. Regardless of their status and ethnic differences, the residents here merged into a unified force against the enemy to guard the culture hidden in this small town.",
  str_loading_h_desc73 = "These knights of the borderlands are different from those in Lumopolis. They roll around so much on the battlefield that sand stained the white silk they wore into a different color from Lumopolis. They are more accustomed to following the edge of their swords than kneeling to the crown.",
  str_loading_h_desc74 = [[
The Colossus that crashed here is so huge.
It once soared freely with wings that could cover the skies.
But now it looks in the direction of Eraveil, fated never to return there.]],
  str_loading_h_desc75 = [[
A Colossus equipped with giant screens and audio equipment from top to bottom.
Archaeologists claim that when celebrating their festivals, the Caelestites would fly Eulogoz into the sky and broadcast celebratory songs and images of dancing across Eraveil.
However, according to the remaining data, Eulogoz and its navigator disappeared mysteriously together about a hundred years ago.]],
  str_loading_h_desc76 = [[
A wondrous beast that can live forever.
There is very little historical information about the Ouroboros, and many extrozoologists indeed believe that the Ouroboros is, in fact, a mere fabrication.
However, Vic firmly believes that it exists and believes that some inexplicable connection exists between himself and this wondrous beast.]],
  str_loading_h_desc77 = [[
An Ouroboros inside its egg can weave dreams according to its own will and make the dreams cycle continuously until it passes through its long incubation period safely.
In the past, people with ulterior motives have deliberately broke into the dream of an Ouroboros to try and stop it from hatching so that they could achieve eternal life in its dream, but they all failed without exception.
That's why you should think twice before entering the dream of an Ouroboros.]],
  str_loading_h_desc78 = "The Shadowind moors at Twin Pavilions Bay and brings glad tidings to the Longzhou natives that dwell there. The route the Shadowind sails connects Longzhou and Astra and has become an important line for mutual cultural exchange and trade between the two regions. These ships travel to and fro, laden with unique goods, delicacies, and treasures of Longzhou, and provide long sought-after passage home for those who had been stranded far from home.",
  str_loading_h_desc79 = "The sea doesn't surrender when facing a well-prepared army, nor does it show mercy to a fish flapping its tail. When the storm strikes, you simply experience the infinite years of its existence in a single moment. When in the very center of the tempest, sailors often pray to the serpentfish, wishing to befall similar fates, to plunge fearlessly into the ocean's depths and then move safely to the shallows of their hometown.",
  str_loading_h_desc80 = "The sunken ship lies quietly on the ocean floor, more serene in this moment than any of the times it floated out on the waves. The sea swallows all sound, drowning out cries for life and leaving only a vision of the end—a faded photograph washed upon the shore. The sea is boundless. There may be many ship graveyards like this, but no one pays tribute to those graves. Those are the cries that have been missed by the world.",
  str_loading_h_desc81 = "To reach his level and judge what he has done or not done would be ridiculous. He doesn't have to explain anything to anyone, so all of his problems are his alone, and his attitude is all that matters. He feels no regret; instead, something more callous—guilt. Using one person to offset the sins of a hundred people... his guilt comes at no choice of his own, yet gives him peace of conscience.",
  str_loading_h_desc82 = [[
When it comes to celebrating Mooncrown Day, there are different customs around the continent.
In Illumina, they are relatively low-key and pragmatic. They express their love by giving cinnamon rolls to their sweethearts.
In Lumopolis, they focus more on the sense of ceremony, and give each other precious red clovers to represent their sincerity.
In Northland, they celebrate simply, gifting small bottles filled with water from Lake Mirror as keepsakes, representing pure love.]],
  str_loading_h_desc83 = [[
A meticulously woven dreamcatcher, an exquisite topaz pendant, a tapestry that was once a collectible among the nobility...
It feels as though you are entering an exquisite antique shop instead of a Courier Union office.
Everything here seems to demonstrate that the owner of this room has exceptional taste.
Most people in the Rediesel Desert are fanatically frugal, but Jeriah demands only the best in terms of quality of life and aesthetic standards.]],
  str_loading_h_desc84 = [[
The central region of the Rediesel Desert is dotted with oases, like stars within a vast galaxy of red sand.
The precious waters of the desert have nurtured countless lives, yet given rise to unimaginable terrors, among which the most famous is the sandworm.
These giants are always lurking in the sand in wait, ready to attack anything that passes by.]],
  str_loading_h_desc85 = [[
According to customs across the continent, Mooncrown Day is a day for lovers to express their sentiments, so many people hold weddings on this day.
To the more traditional nobles, couriers deliver happiness to weddings. Some even spend excessive amounts of money inviting these messengers to attend.
In order to deter this kind of behavior, which severely affects the work efficiency of the continent's couriers, the Courier Union has been promoting other activities in an attempt to phase out this tradition gradually.]],
  str_loading_h_desc86 = "Under the advisement of Schwartz, the Hall of Justice has opened a temporary division to deal with recent love disputes at this special time of the year in order to ensure the seriousness of the main court's trials. Entering the Romance Division is like sitting in a carriage whose wheels will not stop spinning. Before the judge's gavel falls, make sure you bring the most critical evidence to light.",
  str_loading_h_desc87 = "The enthusiasm for Mooncrown Day has clearly not yet subsided in Lumopolis, as a group of Mooncrown enthusiasts is holding an impromptu love salon. Marked by the launch of moon-shaped hot air balloons, both commoners and nobles alike gather under the moon to dance, mingle, and enjoy the hymns of the season. This is also when both ephemeral and eternal feelings can blossom in the blink of an eye.",
  str_loading_h_desc88 = "There is no one in Lumopolis who does not know the Stairway to the Skies. With all the people passing by and visiting this place, countless roads lead to the Stairway to the Skies, you will always find yourself walking on one of them. In this distinctly stratified city, this long stairway carries many meanings beyond a simple \"path.\" When climbing those steps as a child, one can see the stars; when climbing them as an adult, one can even reach Lumopolis Gardens.",
  str_loading_h_desc89 = "Let us rethink what \"justice\" means. It has no precise definition. Generally, most people believe that \"justice\" means doing the right things. These people elect representatives to speak for them, and these representatives condense their opinions into votes. Have you discovered the inevitable outcome of this system? The structure of our society is doomed to define \"justice\" by the number of votes cast, so now, I am \"justice.\"",
  str_loading_h_desc90 = [[
At the behest of the Shadowlord, the Umbraton Orphanage has been rebuilt upon its original site.
Just like the Umbraton of the past, the old orphanage was a cesspool of corruption, bereft of the faintest flicker of hope.
The fire razed the past, and the sun shone fearlessly upon the new soil beneath.]],
  str_loading_h_desc91 = [[
Hati grew up here with her mother.
Although she was not allowed to go outside, she had a happy childhood, bathed in maternal love.
The pony her mother sewed for her was her only playmate as a child, and her colorful picture book was the brimming treasure trove of her imagination.
But now, everything is gone.]],
  str_loading_h_desc92 = [[
The Undercity was once unregistered and unnamed, but it was taken over and rebuilt by someone many years ago.
It was later renamed "Undercity X" and then "Institute X" after a series of research facilities were established.
Unfortunately, the place was eventually destroyed by a fire.]],
  str_loading_h_desc93 = [[
Under the jurisdiction of Professor Ulysses of Illumina, the Archive stores numerous confidential information.
The weight of history behind each thin piece of data is unknown, leaving the true depth of secrets buried.]],
  str_loading_h_desc94 = [[
The most effective modification method discovered thus far is to combine various enhancement methods that have been proven successful on the same experimental subject.
We only need a strong mind to produce a successful outcome.]],
  str_loading_h_desc95 = [[
The Military Exercise aims to provide a stage for all participants to learn, cooperate, and compete.
There are two stages: course preparation and final assessment.
The winning team will have the opportunity to participate in an exhibition match with the Grand Marshal of Illumina.]],
  str_loading_h_desc96 = [[
The meaning of victory in battle should never be doubted.
The battle embodies every Aurorian's persistence, responsibility, and unwavering heroism in the face of darkness as we strive to uphold the light of hope without faltering.]],
  str_loading_h_desc97 = [[
A special crystal ball developed by Boaz, a legendary divination master of Northland.
Once activated with Lumina, it automatically records all events that occur within a certain range of the activator throughout the day.
The activator only needs to inject it with Lumina once more to transport themselves or those they touch into the Crystal of Eternal Memory and revisit what happened on that day.]],
  str_loading_h_desc98 = [[
In order to commemorate the Schwartz family's contribution to Lumopolis, the people of the city spontaneously decided to hold a celebration on the day the first ancestor of the Schwartz family became the City Lord. Over time, this day became an official holiday of Lumopolis.
The Schwartz family consistently holds parades, celebrations, social dinners, and other events on this day.
However, since the Darkover Crisis, the scale of the festivities has gradually waned.]],
  str_loading_h_desc99 = [[
Thousands of years ago, the ancestors of the Kartima family signed a contract with the dragons.
For millennia, the awakened Dragonkin have welcomed their own dragons, vowing to forever be loyal to one another and unconditionally sacrifice their lives and power for each other.
However, in order to blend into Aurorian society, the Kartima family came to regard the awakened Dragonkin as outsiders and forbade them from reproducing. Why their attitudes changed so suddenly is still yet to be answered. The only thing that can be confirmed is that Mime Kartima, the leader of the family, summoned the dragons again. But from that day on, their family began to decline completely.]],
  str_loading_h_desc100 = "\"You may have many questions in your mind, and I can't guarantee to have all the answers. This journey is meant to be short, so I urge you to treasure this fleeting experience above all else.\"",
  str_loading_h_desc101 = [[
Born in family of highly-educated individuals, Joshua is a remarkable and knowledgeable woman who excels at academics and fighting. Her father was a well-known scholar who tutored Daniel when he was young. That's how they met and eventually became a couple who overcame the class barrier. The story of their love is a classic of the new era of Lumopolis, which inspires countless young men and women with longing and expectations for the future. Joshua lived up to the people's expectations, presenting herself with an image as perfect as the Holy Mother, which greatly increased the people's political trust in the Schwartz family.
That's how things were until that accident.]],
  str_loading_h_desc102 = [[
She once had a name of her own, but now she is called Joshua or the Child of Montague. Unlike the incumbent City Lord, the former City Lord, Daniel's father, was a tyrant. Through unprecedented tyranny, he changed the class that had reinforced its views in Lumopolis for a hundred years and also purged his opponents extremely cruelly. Joshua is a survivor of House Montague.
Some conspirators made an argument based on these survivors to establish an organization with the goal of bringing down the Schwartz family. However, it was just another political struggle for more power, and no one really cared about the grief of the survivors. The unsatiable anger in their eyes is just a tool in the eyes of others.]],
  str_loading_h_desc103 = [[
Denuo Wonderland, located deep within the Rediesel Desert and embraced by a serene gorge, marks the first phase of Denuo Valley Resort's development.
The Rediesel Wrench played a significant role in designing several attractions during the park's establishment, ensuring an exhilarating and challenging experience for all visitors. It's worth noting that the sky wheel remains open during the night, allowing guests to enjoy a romantic fireworks display while riding it.]],
  str_loading_h_desc104 = [[
Nestled next to the wonderland, the Denuo Resort Hotel presents itself as a magnificent castle gracefully arising from the wonderland.
The distinctive gardening landscape at the front entrance embodies the cultural essence of Denuo Valley and the developers' profound respect for nature. Noteworthy are the handcrafted artifacts displayed in the hotel's grand lobby and terrace, crafted by local artisans showcasing their extraordinary talents. The entire hotel is like a museum, recounting the fascinating history of Denuo Valley and the enchanting legend of the Denuo Goddess for every valued guest.]],
  str_loading_h_desc105 = [[
Denuo Valley stands as a pristine gem, boasting an advantageous geographical layout and picturesque natural scenery.
As local legends recount, a mysterious natural disaster once struck the gorge, wiping out an entire village. This event served as a profound reminder of nature, prompting developers to prioritize eco-conscious restoration and preservation throughout the development process. Now, Denuo Valley thrives as a flourishing sanctuary, providing a harmonious haven for abundant fascinating wildlife and plants.]],
  str_loading_h_desc106 = [[
Denuo Valley Resort Hotel is equipped with cutting-edge air purification systems. To minimize noises generated during air circulation, the resort's owner followed the staff's advice and constructed an underground chamber to accommodate the sizeable machinery.
Little do they know, behind a secret door in the room, there's a mysterious and hidden tunnel. Stored within are items that seem to carry a distant and fascinating history.]],
  str_loading_h_desc107 = [[
The history of Illumina Prison spans through the ages, established with the initial goal of upholding federation security, penalizing criminal behavior, and fostering introspection and reform among offenders.
Inmates are classified into different categories and levels within the prison based on their degree of danger, the nature of their crimes, and the duration of their sentences. Typically, the committee directly appoints the management crew of high-security prisons. Anyone entering these high-security facilities must provide valid documentation.]],
  str_loading_h_desc108 = [[
Lumo Stronghold is home to the earliest exiles from Lumopolis, including knights, residents, and their descendants, all governed by local nobles from Lumopolis. The present City Lord, Dietrich, has amassed wealth in recent years through the mining of ores and has established an army, granting him considerable influence over the surface towns of Lumopolis.
Within Lumo Stronghold, there's an independent church and infrastructure sector, which, during times of war, are committed to protecting Lumopolis residents.]],
  str_loading_h_desc109 = [[
Released by the Eclipsite Mudbundle, the tainted mud sweeps across the land like an obsidian tide. Wherever it touches the earth, a fierce corrosive hiss erupts, followed by ground crumbling and plants withering. A powerful stench of decay lingers in the air as the mire expands rapidly, ensnaring innocent beings within its grasp.
Mudbundle lurks within the depths of the mud, capable of agile movement and attacks against Aurorians. The Eclipsites, on the other hand, harness the Darkflow within the mud to enhance their offensive prowess.]],
  str_loading_h_desc110 = [[
As far as we know, the Warp is likely a potent Darkflow stemming from the Eclipse. Each time a team caught in it advances a certain distance, they always find themselves back to the starting point. The exact nature of this art is shrouded in mystery.
This 'starting point' refers to the center of a fixed circular space, constraining the party's movement within its radius. This leaves the Aurorians with a constant feeling of running in circles, trapped even in an illusion of infinite loops.]],
  str_loading_h_desc111 = [[
Lumo Stronghold is home to the earliest exiles from Lumopolis, including knights, residents, and their descendants, all governed by local nobles from Lumopolis. The present City Lord, Dietrich, has amassed wealth in recent years through the mining of ores and has established an army, granting him considerable influence over the surface towns of Lumopolis.
Within Lumo Stronghold, there's an independent church and infrastructure sector, which, during times of war, are committed to protecting Lumopolis residents.]],
  str_loading_h_desc112 = [[
The design of Illumina Prison cells adheres to established standards and amenities, ensuring effective inmate supervision and safety measures. Each cell provides storage space for convicts to secure personal belongings, ranging from small to medium-sized containers, clothing, and reading materials. Lighting and ventilation fixtures are also in place for comfort and security within the cell.
Regular inspections and maintenance are imperative for prison cells, ensuring the sustained upkeep of safety and hygiene standards. Rumors suggest that this facility also detains criminals from other factions.]],
  str_loading_h_desc113 = "A domain that transcends the realm of material entities, seemingly reachable only through unique pathways. The leaders of the True Order claim to have received revelations from the Lord of Truth at this very location.\nWithin this secret territory, differentiation between light and darkness becomes elusive, as something shimmering in crimson appears to substitute the usual air medium, causing the Aurorians arriving here for the first time to experience indescribable sensations—body suspension, intense compression, and beyond.",
  str_loading_N33_Cname_01 = "Denuo Wonderland",
  str_loading_N33_Cname_02 = "Resort Hotel",
  str_loading_N33_Cname_03 = "Denuo Valley",
  str_loading_N33_Cname_04 = "Basement",
  str_loading_N33_Ename_01 = "A deluxe wonderland nestled deep within the Rediesel Desert.",
  str_loading_N33_Ename_02 = "An ultra-luxurious hotel resort.",
  str_loading_N33_Ename_03 = "An undeveloped canyon region within Denuo Valley Resort.",
  str_loading_N33_Ename_04 = "An underground basement at the hotel, housing ventilation equipment and soundproofing measures.",
  str_loading_N33_des_01 = [[
Denuo Wonderland, located deep within the Rediesel Desert and embraced by a serene gorge, marks the first phase of Denuo Valley Resort's development.
The Rediesel Wrench played a significant role in designing several attractions during the park's establishment, ensuring an exhilarating and challenging experience for all visitors. As a special treat, once the sun sets, all guests are invited to take the sky wheel and catch a super romantic fireworks show!]],
  str_loading_N33_des_02 = [[
Nestled next to the Denuo Wonderland, the Denuo Resort Hotel presents itself as a magnificent castle gracefully arising from the wonderland.
The distinctive gardening landscape at the front entrance embodies the cultural essence of Denuo Valley and the developers' profound respect for nature. Noteworthy are the handcrafted artifacts displayed in the hotel's grand lobby and terrace, crafted by local artisans showcasing their extraordinary talents. As a whole, the hotel resembles a miniature museum, narrating the tale of Denuo Village's rich history and the legend of the Denuo Goddess for each cherished guest.]],
  str_loading_N33_des_03 = [[
Denuo Valley stands as a pristine gem, boasting an advantageous geographical layout and picturesque natural scenery.
As local legends recount, a mysterious natural disaster once struck the gorge, wiping out an entire village. This event served as a profound reminder of nature, prompting developers to prioritize eco-conscious restoration and preservation throughout the development process. Now, Denuo Valley thrives as a flourishing sanctuary, providing a harmonious haven for abundant fascinating wildlife and plants.]],
  str_loading_N33_des_04 = [[
Denuo Valley Resort Hotel is equipped with cutting-edge air purification systems. To minimize noises generated during air circulation, the resort's owner followed the staff's advice and constructed an underground chamber to accommodate the sizeable machinery.
Little do they know, behind a secret door in the room, there's a mysterious and hidden tunnel. Stored within are items that seem to carry a distant and fascinating history.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10004 = [[
Eve was born and raised in the Rediesel Desert.
She lives in a caravan community with her robust father and caring mother.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10005 = [[
Eve's always wondered about the street's odd name... it's fine, though.
It's got cool shops and the doc's clinic.
That's all that matters!]],
  str_loading_h_desc10006 = [[
In Eve's memory, she'd never been elsewhere beyond the caravan area and Tail Street.
Now, having busted open the iron gate to the outside world herself, her parents would probably give her a serious lesson if they knew.
Plus... see, the outside world is pretty scary indeed.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10007 = [[
The scenery shifts continuously before her eyes, like a beautiful but intangible fairy tale, abruptly baring its fiery fangs.
The illusion will crumble like mountains eventually, so keep pressing on...]],
  str_loading_h_desc20011 = [[
"Since childhood, Irridon has harbored a deep-seated desire to work within the Hall of Justice.
As for the specific reasons... it seems even Irridon herself has difficulty recalling them."]],
  str_loading_h_desc20012 = [[
"Noble families of lofty stature usually do not send their offspring to Dawn Academy for studies; instead, they prefer to engage the services of the most exceptional private tutors.
Irridon's father, however, deviated from the norm. He hoped Irridon could learn early on how to stand out among the masses."]],
  str_loading_h_desc20013 = [[
"From Irridon's home within the Lumopolis Gardens, it's a few twists and turns followed by a journey down the long Stairway to the Skies to reach the Lumopolis Courtyard.
In Irridon's eyes, the Courtyard doesn't seem all that distinct from the Gardens.
Yet, for many of Irridon's fellow students during her school days, scaling the staircase between the Courtyard class and the Gardens class was like mission impossible."]],
  str_loading_h_desc20014 = [[
"During Irridon's early years, she had scarce opportunities to venture into the Lower Lumopolis.
According to her father, that place was teeming with uncouth minor nobles and common folks, which he concerned might negatively influence the child."]],
  str_loading_h_desc20015 = [[
Upon the tranquil surface of the water, concentric rings of golden ripples form one after another.
The reflections in the water gradually contort by the ripples, almost like there's a whole fantastical and colorful world in there.]],
  str_loading_h_desc20028 = [[
Northland is the cradle of Aurorians and countless tales.
It's said that the Morning Calendar began when the first Beacon was lit.
Before that, stories lost to the darkness are said to rest here.]],
  str_loading_h_desc20029 = [[
The wonderland of many Caelestites is now a home for just one person.
They say many Caelestites ventured out from here.
Only to spend their whole lives trying to come back.]],
  str_loading_h_desc20030 = [[
The Caelestites dry their tears and bid farewell to the lost ones on this very day.
They smile and release Dandelion Lanterns with wishes.
They craft Windelion Dolls to symbolize their will to move forward.
It's not about forgetting but using their memories as fuel to keep going.]],
  str_loading_h_desc20031 = "Even in the frozen wilderness, there's this miraculous place.\nThose who had survived the bitter cold planted seeds of wonderland here.\nMaybe—\nEven after going through countless twists of fate, their hearts still bloom with hope.",
  str_loading_h_desc80030001 = "Connolly prefers to call the place \"residence\" rather than \"home.\"",
  str_loading_h_desc80030002 = "The streets seem to be enveloped in an ethereal mist under the rippling, sprinkling light, with aqua lives and residents resembling fishes roaming through them.",
  str_loading_h_desc80030003 = "Compared to the dim and cold attic, the place invigorated Connolly and brought her warmth and support. To Connolly, there is finally a sense of belonging and a place to return to.",
  str_loading_h_desc80030004 = [[
Here, a fantastic town located under the deep sea that resembles the wonderland in fairy tales.
Connolly immerses herself in this aqua world, and will she manage to navigate through tumultuous undercurrents and meet with close friends?]],
  str_loading_h_desc80040001 = "The west side of Twin Pavilions Bay is managed by Umbraton. This area is similar to other cities of Astra in terms of architectural style, but it looks more exotic due to the addition of Longzhou decorations.",
  str_loading_h_desc80040002 = "The east side of Twin Pavilions Bay is under the jurisdiction of the Lin Guild, and there is a Little Longzhou district, which is designed to look just like Longzhou, next to the port.",
  str_loading_h_desc80040003 = "Twin Pavilions Bay has several ports with a large number of docks and ships. It shoulders the important responsibility of shipping operations between Astra and Longzhou and is always ready to receive ships and cargo from all over the world.",
  str_loading_h_desc80040004 = "A long, long time ago, there was a weak, cursed swordfighter who wielded a big sword that could defeat any demon and vanquish any enemy. The swordfighter was not moved by money or fame and was on a single-minded quest to find and break all kinds of strange curses. Will she be able to usher in her own dawn after slaying all the curses of the world?",
  str_loading_h_desc80050001 = "A courageous and humorous hero rising from civilians, leader of the Northwind Legion who always willingly sacrifices himself for the kingdom and its people. But has anyone truly delved into his heart to understand the burdens he carries, his millennia-old anguish?",
  str_loading_h_desc80050002 = "Before this land came to be known as Astra, it harbored scattered buds of the Aurorian civilizations. Among them was a kingdom, its traces long weathered into dust, yet its legends endure till today.",
  str_loading_h_desc80050003 = "Towering in the city's center, a majestic structure enshrines the shared beliefs of everyone in the kingdom. Unlike today's Lumopolis, this sacred place did not reject impoverished refugees a thousand years ago.",
  str_loading_h_desc80050004 = "Only true warriors can step into the arena, showcasing their might before the crowd, embracing a shower of flowers and cheers...",
  str_loading_N35_Cname_01 = "Underground Ruins",
  str_loading_N35_Cname_02 = "Northland",
  str_loading_N35_Cname_03 = "Zarya",
  str_loading_N35_Ename_01 = "Ruins from an ancient era.",
  str_loading_N35_Ename_02 = "The Land of Ice and Snow, Origin of the Aurorians",
  str_loading_N35_Ename_03 = "Frozen Maiden",
  str_loading_N35_des_01 = "This location does not exist on any map and is absent from most explorers' guidebooks. These ruins are filled with countless dangers, as though defying all who approach from advancing further. It almost feels like the deeper you go, the more distinctly you can hear a mechanical sound, devoid of all emotion, and terrifying enough to make any intruder turn tail and run. If you continue moving forward, what will you find in the depths?",
  str_loading_N35_des_02 = "Northland was born in the snow, and endures through the frost. Under the Queen's guardianship, Aurorians have guarded Northland for generations. Now, as in the past, even if they must sacrifice their lives or face unimaginable loneliness, they never shirk this responsibility. But bear in mind, although Northland is the birthplace of the Aurorians, it is not the birthplace of all civilization.",
  str_loading_N35_des_03 = "A hundred years is longer than a lifetime for most Aurorians, but for Zarya, the sorrows and regrets of a century past seem like yesterday. Imprisoned within this unyielding tomb of ice for a hundred years, she was finally liberated. However, who will deliver her from the icy frost and the lingering doubts frozen deep within her heart?",
  str_loading_N36_Cname_01 = "Umbraton",
  str_loading_N36_Cname_02 = "Illumina Outpost",
  str_loading_N36_Cname_03 = "Rediesel Desert",
  str_loading_N36_Ename_01 = "\"A hub of business and intel.\"",
  str_loading_N36_Ename_02 = "\"Repel the enemies, embrace the like-minded.\"",
  str_loading_N36_Ename_03 = "\"Desert, the true realm of freedom.\"",
  str_loading_N36_des_01 = "Located beneath Lumopolis City, Umbraton is a hub of commerce and finance but also harbors crimes, corruption, and deception. However, as you interact with the locals, you will discover that not everyone in Umbraton is morally bankrupt. There are some genuinely good folks here, like the owner of Liu's Restaurant and the boss of Cloudrover Guild.",
  str_loading_N36_des_02 = "This is a crucial area for defending against the Eclipsites. The soldiers stationed here are responsible for not only repelling Eclipsite attacks but also safeguarding Illumina and conducting routine patrols of nearby regions and trade routes. From time to time, these soldiers host celebration feasts. Regardless of your origins, as long as you haven't caused trouble before or have aided Illumina, they'll extend an invitation to you.",
  str_loading_N36_des_03 = "Within the vast expanse of the Rediesel Desert, you'll encounter many peculiar creatures other than Eclipsites, and you might even catch a glimpse of the legendary dragons. But still, when people mention the Rediesel Desert, the first thing that comes to mind is the Rediesel Wrench led by Sinsa. Its members frequently traverse the desert in their vehicles, living a carefree and enjoyable life.",
  str_loading_c_h_name10001 = "Twin Pavilions Bay",
  str_loading_c_h_name10002 = "Harbor of Twin Pavilions Bay",
  str_loading_e_h_name10001 = "A pivotal harbor connecting Astra and Longzhou.",
  str_loading_e_h_name10002 = [[
This bustling harbor never sleeps, with merchant ships docking round the clock.
These vessels, laden with the tangible weight of people's hopes and dreams, punctuate the ebb and flow of life here.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10001 = [[
Cradled at the mouth of the Gold River, Twin Pavilions Bay was once a mere whisper of a town. Its destiny was irrevocably altered years ago with the arrival of the first merchant ship from Longzhou, initiating its transformation into a vibrant metropolis.
The city is a remarkable study in contrasts: the eastern half, nestled against the sea and port, is under the stewardship of the Lin Guild, its architectural veins pulsing with the Longzhou style; the western half, run by Umbraton, presents a mirror image of Umbraton in its cityscape.]],
  str_loading_h_desc10002 = [[
The Harbor of Twin Pavilions Bay, shaped by the ceaseless tide of merchant ships, has a tapestry of streets that echo the Longzhou style, alive with the heartbeat of the marketplace.
Small shops, serving primarily as a haven for sailors, punctuate the landscape, interspersed with affordable eateries, inns, and occasional street vendors.
The Golden Bridge, a distant silhouette thought, functions as a unifying thread between the eastern and western halves of the city.]],
  str_loading_N37_Cname_01 = "Cloudrover Guild",
  str_loading_N37_Cname_02 = "Nameless Clinic",
  str_loading_N37_Cname_03 = "Black Wolves",
  str_loading_N37_Ename_01 = "One of the most prosperous and famous guilds in Umbraton",
  str_loading_N37_Ename_02 = "Trusted underground clinic",
  str_loading_N37_Ename_03 = "Rapidly emerging gang in Umbraton",
  str_loading_N37_des_01 = "A guild founded by Sheol.\nIn a short few years, it grew from a mobile store that nobody knew into one of the top guilds in Umbraton.\nThe Cloudrover Guild didn't achieve that feat for no reason. After all, you can buy anything you can imagine—and beyond—here.\nEven you have been lost among its selections, haven't you?",
  str_loading_N37_des_02 = [[
A small clinic in the remote slums of Umbraton that no one knew when it first opened.
The doctor and assistant never revealed their names, so everyone just called them "Nameless Doctor" and "Nameless Assistant."
Despite the mystery, the poor folks nearby still seek treatment in droves, given how inexpensive and good the doctor is.]],
  str_loading_N37_des_03 = [[
In Umbraton, countless small gangs have formed out of the necessity for self-protection, though ones that not only have carved a name out but continue to expand like the Black Wolves are far and few between.
Some claim the Black Wolves have the backing of a certain major guild to act as brazen as they do, but the gang never gives a straight answer to that rumor.
Perhaps, it is just because no one has ever asked that question out in the open.]],
  str_loading_N38_Cname_01 = "Twin Pavilions Bay",
  str_loading_N38_Cname_02 = "Shadowind",
  str_loading_N38_Ename_01 = "Bicontinental Commerce Harbor",
  str_loading_N38_Ename_02 = "Mechanized Ocean Vessel",
  str_loading_N38_des_01 = "Originally a small fishing village on the east side of Umbraton, it has evolved into a trading port with the arrival of Longzhou merchant ships. Nowadays, the western side of the current Twin Pavilions Bay is managed by Umbraton, sharing architectural styles with other Astra cities. The eastern side is under the Lin Guild's control, featuring an eastern-themed street and harbor akin to Longzhou's style.",
  str_loading_N38_des_02 = [[
A cutting-edge ocean vessel funded and constructed by the Lin Guild.
Designed with the addition of Ye Kingdom's machinery, it surpasses traditional ships in durability and power. Additionally, it boasts a device for underwater salvage operations. This vessel will transport navigators, Xuan Ji, and others into the deep sea, venturing into unexplored realms.]],
  str_loading_N39_Cname_01 = "Cloudrover Guild",
  str_loading_N39_Cname_02 = "The Pit",
  str_loading_N39_Cname_03 = "Continental Guild",
  str_loading_N39_Ename_01 = "One of the most prosperous and famous guilds in Umbraton",
  str_loading_N39_Ename_02 = "A place of entertainment for the nobility.",
  str_loading_N39_Ename_03 = "An up-and-coming guild based outside of Umbraton.",
  str_loading_N39_des_01 = [[
A guild founded by Sheol. In just a few short years, it expanded from a nameless mobile shop to one of Umbraton's most powerful guilds.
Today, the Cloudrover Guild even possesses a massive airship that incorporates travel, shopping, leisure, and vacationing, all in one place!
The Cloudrover Guild's capacity for such grand achievements is not without reason. After all, any product imaginable (and even unimaginable) can be purchased through them.
Even you have gotten lost in its sizeable selections, haven't you?]],
  str_loading_N39_des_02 = [[
On the surface between Umbraton and Lumopolis exists a large swath of land once known as "The Pit." Long ago, it served as a theater of blood sport for the nobles of Lumopolis.
Here, they would cast one hundred hardened criminals into The Pit, and force them to slaughter one another for their amusement; the last person standing would receive a full pardon, as well as lavish rewards from the noble who sponsored them. In time, a number of fighters emerged from Umbraton, gladiators who voluntarily entered The Pit in search of wealth and glory.
Before the Darkover Crisis, the nobles had already begun slowly retreating to the safety of Lumopolis, and The Pit fell into decline; nevertheless, its culture of "strength above all" persisted and became the status quo in Umbraton. Soon, illegal fight rings seeking to imitate the glory of The Pit sprung up all over the city, garnering massive amounts of attention.]],
  str_loading_N39_des_03 = [[
A large-scale guild that has emerged outside of Umbraton. Its leader is a mysterious woman who rarely shows her face in public.
Guilds rarely see this level of rapid growth without relying on Umbraton's geographical and logistical advantages, yet the Continental Guild managed to achieve it somehow.
As its name suggests, the Continental Guild's influence stretches to almost every small town and village in the land of Astra.]],
  str_loading_c_h_name121 = "Algol's Lab",
  str_loading_c_h_name122 = "Old Illumina Chamber",
  str_loading_c_h_name123 = "Above Gannon City",
  str_loading_c_h_name124 = "Warehouse Zero",
  str_loading_c_h_name125 = "Unknown Fissure",
  str_loading_c_h_name126 = "Pristine River",
  str_loading_e_h_name121 = "An Illumina office that's both high-tech and accommodating.",
  str_loading_e_h_name122 = "An old Illumina lab mired in suspicions and controversies.",
  str_loading_e_h_name123 = "Like dawn, yet like sunset.",
  str_loading_e_h_name124 = "A mysterious off-record warehouse in Illumina.",
  str_loading_e_h_name125 = "Shattered sinking fissure of unknown depth and darkness.",
  str_loading_e_h_name126 = "Twisting, glistening river with enigmatic charm.",
  str_loading_h_desc121 = [[
This mixed-architecture lab is Illumina scientist Algol's private office. Such a venue combining both technology and comfort is rare in the military-dominated Gannon.
While the lab is not compliant with The Illumina Regulations for Living Quarters Management, no one objected since most of the furniture was built by Algol using recycled materials. It is said that anyone visiting the lab could sleep soundly to the electronic buzzes in the background.]],
  str_loading_h_desc122 = [[
Many years ago when supplies were scarce in the Illumina Federation, young, idealistic scientists discussed the future of Aurorians day and night in this small lab.
If there was an end to the Aurorians, every such discussion and question raised was to stop that from happening. However, the lab tables, floor and steel frameworks that once were the reflections of that wisdom have since disappeared.]],
  str_loading_h_desc123 = [[
When someone in Illumina looks upward in the undercity, they know the penetrating ray of light is a gift from the "civilized world" to Gannon. Time after time, Gannon has endured Eclipsite raids, thus the people of Illumina endeavor to repel the invaders, hoping one day they can resurface and enjoy the sunshine in peace.
However, this ray is also the final farewell from the civilized world. With the Darkover Crisis imminent, will Illumina hold on to their home?]],
  str_loading_h_desc124 = [[
A copious, empty, chilly warehouse pungent with the scent of solutions. The open space seems to once hold enormous yet lethal weapons. Those who set foot inside for the first time have never felt themselves more insignificant.
A continuously running machine acts like a link between the past and present. Approach the intricate, squeaking biological lab table and you can almost hear the cries of the countless innocent lives who welcomed their "rebirth" here.]],
  str_loading_h_desc125 = [[
A giant fissure without any sign of life. Judging from the cracks, it's an ancient Dark Zone phenomenon. Violent explosions in the past were also evident, leaving only a pitch-black pit, drifting pebbles and charred earth. On the surface, the cracks are branching out even farther.
What happened here? Or, what is still happening?]],
  str_loading_h_desc126 = [[
Endless darkness and quiet as if time has stood still. Suddenly, an inscrutable river slowly spans from the remote "horizon" like in a painting. This is a fantasy landscape never before seen on Astra maps. Its appearance shrouds the world's reality in even more mystery.
Where is the source of this river? Is it real? Why is it that when you stir the water, unexpected changes happen somewhere in the world?]],
  str_loading_c_h_name127 = "Ji Kingdom",
  str_loading_c_h_name128 = "Coastal Crisis in Ji Kingdom",
  str_loading_c_h_name129 = "Spring Festival",
  str_loading_e_h_name127 = "Kingdom of Water Commerce and Shipping",
  str_loading_e_h_name128 = "Dragon Maiden, Eclipsites, and the Seal",
  str_loading_e_h_name129 = "Longzhou New Year",
  str_loading_h_desc127 = "A vassal kingdom in western Longzhou. It is filled with many crisscrossing rivers, and as such, it has a well-developed water transportation system with ship routes throughout most parts of Longzhou, making it a transportation hub since ancient times. As commercial trade flourished, it naturally became the center of the economy. Its capital, Haojin City, is extremely prosperous and is home to many wealthy merchant families, including the Lin Guild.",
  str_loading_h_desc128 = "Hundreds of years ago, the remnants of Eclipsites buried in the coastal waters of Ji Kingdom once corrupted the Dragon Maiden's kin, a black serpentine dragon. The Dragon Maiden had to severely damage it, sealing the sea cave to prevent the overflow of Eclipsite power. Due to the kingdom's negligence over the grand ritual, the seal has been destroyed, freeing Eclipsites to stir chaos. The Ji Kingdom, though mobilized its force to respond, has experienced substantial losses.",
  str_loading_h_desc129 = "Spring Festival is the most important festival on the Longzhou Continent. The royal family would host banquets for esteemed guests while the citizens gathered for leisure and catch-up. In the Ji Kingdom, the locals organize temple fairs, pay homage to the Dragon Maiden, and drive away the Nian beast during the festival, hoping for health and good fortune in the coming year. Some merchants hire fiendlings to put on shows themed on the beast-chasing ritual, adding a touch of fun to the beginning of the new year.",
  str_loading_c_h_name205 = "Illumina Federation Aircraft Control Room",
  str_loading_c_h_name206 = "Snowbound Border",
  str_loading_c_h_name207 = "Borderland Cavern",
  str_loading_c_h_name208 = "Ancestral Altar",
  str_loading_c_h_name209 = "Castle Ramparts",
  str_loading_e_h_name205 = "Cold and imposing, with a rich scent of metal lingering in the air.",
  str_loading_e_h_name206 = "The rarely visited northwest frontier of Northland.",
  str_loading_e_h_name207 = "An ancient cavern veiled by layers of ice.",
  str_loading_e_h_name208 = "The mysterious sacred ground guarded by generations of the Snow Fox tribe.",
  str_loading_e_h_name209 = "An ancient castle ravaged by warfare.",
  str_loading_h_desc205 = "While not as spacious as the Control Room of the Colossus, this place is enough to accommodate a medium-sized expedition team. Its walls are covered with intricate instrument panels and screens, accurately recording various parameters and data of the aircraft. As the pointers on the instrument panel constantly oscillate, the faint rhythmic mechanical sound seems to resonate with the frequency of a giant mechanical calculation deep within an Illumina Undercity.",
  str_loading_h_desc206 = "Under the gloomy sky of snow, the once boundless snowy desert appears to have an end. Tall mountains stand like a wall in the distance, dividing this place from the outside world. Yet, the desolate Snowpine Forest faces another dreadful assault, with houses reduced to rubble, snow pines callously snapped, and the snow stained with large patches of red-black blood... It seems that no one knows or cares about the creatures living here.",
  str_loading_h_desc207 = "The chilling cavern features a labyrinthine and complex structure. Some ice walls tower vertically, while others are low and narrow, forcing passersby to bend over. Dim light filters through ice crystals, casting speckled shadows and draping the cave in a serene, silvery-white shadow. Towering and rugged ice columns, along with ice flowers on the cave walls, shift into peculiar shapes, poised for the moment when the aurora descends.",
  str_loading_h_desc208 = "Within the depths of the dark cavern, shafts of light pierce the ceiling, casting onto the altar below, as if the creators of the altar await the awakening of the three sacred trees. Before the altar stands a stone slab inscribed with ancient runes, detailing the legend of the \"Three Pine Trees.\" Two weathered Snow Fox statues stand sentinel, symbolizing their tribe's guardianship of the altar. The elders once said that despite seeming frozen for millennia, the blessing of the sacred trees endures.",
  str_loading_h_desc209 = "A gust of wind sweeps into the depths of the cave, blowing through a towering ancient castle emerging from the ground. In the raging blizzard, the castle's interior glows brightly with fire. The defenders of the castle move about, their spirits high as they march forward to uphold their ancient vow. Their shouts and the clash of weapons have banished the chill from the ice and snow, making them forget the harshness of this era.",
  str_loading_N45_Cname_01 = "Rediesel Wrench Base",
  str_loading_N45_Cname_02 = "Leyline Corridor",
  str_loading_N45_Cname_03 = "Roaring Volcano",
  str_loading_N45_Ename_01 = [[
A temporary base set up by Rediesel Wrench after they stopped moving.
Efficient and convenient.]],
  str_loading_N45_Ename_02 = [[
A winding path under the Rediesel Desert.
These mysterious passages are connected to the desert leylines.]],
  str_loading_N45_Ename_03 = [[
An underground volcano that is always roaring.
Strangely, it erupted just 15 years ago.]],
  str_loading_N45_des_01 = [[
Due to the harsh environment of the desert, Rediesel Wrench is often forced to leave the oasis to search for supplies.
When Lepidoz stops, they will build a temporary base on the spot.]],
  str_loading_N45_des_02 = [[
Under the Rediesel Desert are many inexplicable winding passages that extend in all directions and are collectively called the leyline corridor.
No one knows how they formed, but the corridor seems to have existed for a long time and was even developed for a while. However, everything was destroyed by the onset of various disasters.]],
  str_loading_N45_des_03 = [[
The Roaring Volcano is the most dangerous volcano in the Rediesel Desert. It is usually dormant, but it always makes a roaring sound. The only time it erupted, it destroyed the original base of the Rediesel Desert.
Members of Rediesel Wrench fear this volcano and haven't returned there in many years.
According to some of the rumors spread among them, the roaring sound belongs to Eclipsites who live in the magma.]],
  str_loading_N46_Cname_01 = "Hidden Fangs",
  str_loading_N46_Ename_01 = [[
Umbraton Arcade.
The symbol of Astra's gaming community.]],
  str_loading_N46_des_01 = "An arcade founded by seasoned gamers. It started out as a small club that served Aurorians who had a soft spot for ancient gaming consoles. As more and more games were restored and developed, gamers from all across Astra were drawn over, and soon the arcade became the gaming community's main hangout.",
  str_loading_N47_Cname_01 = "Base: Surface Level",
  str_loading_N47_Cname_02 = "Base: Passage",
  str_loading_N47_Cname_03 = "Base: Chasm",
  str_loading_N47_Cname_04 = "Base: Ruins",
  str_loading_N47_Cname_05 = "Spearhead",
  str_loading_N47_Ename_01 = "Time and the Foundation Fall Together",
  str_loading_N47_Ename_02 = "Echo of the Abandoned Instrument's Space",
  str_loading_N47_Ename_03 = "The Breaking Point of Memories and Turning Point of Life",
  str_loading_N47_Ename_04 = "Resting Place of the Tattered Colossus Spearhead",
  str_loading_N47_Ename_05 = "Where Phantoms of the Past Linger",
  str_loading_N47_des_01 = [[
An experimental base buried by Illumina. It might have remained hidden if it hadn't been for Barton's immense strength creating an opening.
The fragile foundation forms a stark contrast to Illumina's sturdy city walls of today. Nevertheless, the secrets of the past always bide their time, waiting for the right person to uncover them.
This place has witnessed both passionate training and cruel experiments, as well as desperate struggling and fiery rebellion.]],
  str_loading_N47_des_02 = "The discarded instruments act as guards that obstruct the path of intruders. Several still-functioning instruments peeked out from the ruins, disrupting intruders' thoughts while secretly making plans. This is a dark cave that isolates distressed cries, and a long tunnel that tests dreamers. If you hear a voice calling you, maybe you should stop and see if it is your abandoned past reaching out to you.",
  str_loading_N47_des_03 = "That was a time of unbearable hardship, burying countless abandoned life experiences. Above the chasm is the high ground of the victors, and below it is the graveyard of the sacrificed. Anyone who wishes to overturn this unjust past must plunge into the abyss. Only when their bodies are burning and no flesh remains to be destroyed can they soar forever.",
  str_loading_N47_des_04 = [[
At the very bottom of the experimental base lies a Colossus with a broken tail that still has a faint consciousness.
Its tenacious will seems to be commanding its scattered parts to piece itself together while it waits for a Navigator's command to set off towards its former home. It seems to have been here for longer than the entire history of Illumina, and the truth of this experiment is revealed by all the experimental equipment built around it at a later time.]],
  str_loading_N47_des_05 = [[
This dangerous transaction is the last clue available to all explorers.
Through a special instrument, one can see the remaining master-control room data of Spearhead. Although the room is in ruins, its internal structure is more concise and smooth compared to Soroz, and each control panel exudes a dangerous aura. Did it come from the Dark Zone? Could its Navigator be a Caelestite?]],
  str_loading_N48_Cname_01 = "Varaki Town",
  str_loading_N48_Cname_02 = "Advent of Truth",
  str_loading_N48_Cname_03 = "Tomb of the Varaki",
  str_loading_N48_Cname_04 = "Wilhelm's Castle",
  str_loading_N48_Cname_05 = "Temple of Truth",
  str_loading_N48_Ename_01 = "Homeland of the family of vampire.",
  str_loading_N48_Ename_02 = "Grand assembly of the True Order.",
  str_loading_N48_Ename_03 = "Resting place of the Varaki ancestors.",
  str_loading_N48_Ename_04 = "A cold and solitary castle on the cliffside.",
  str_loading_N48_Ename_05 = "An eerie and sacred crimson hall.",
  str_loading_N48_des_01 = [[
the family of vampire, a distinct Aurorian race, has long inhabited the town of Varaki, as the legends say. They favor the night and have a craving for blood. Their lifespans are extended, often keeping the looks they had at the awakening of their bloodline.
This family's descendants inherit the great power of their ancestors when their bloodline is awakened. However, the painful memories that come with this power are the cost they must bear.]],
  str_loading_N48_des_02 = "Every three years, such a night occurs—At midnight, the bells of the Temple of Truth ring, and the tall bell towers extend and reach up toward the moon.\nThe moon, glowing in blood-red, sits in the sky as if the Lord of Truth is listening to their confessions in the temple and sharing the family's glory and secrets. Disciples of Truth don robes and march with coffins through the streets, reverently chanting the Lord's name, awaiting the Lord of Truth's arrival.",
  str_loading_N48_des_03 = [[
The Varaki clan regards their ancestors' remains as treasures and, at specific times, views them with the family leader and disciples. Moreover, the ancient coffins in the tombs hold many hidden secrets.
Black plants with a mystical glow encircle the tombs, which, in the bloody moonlight, will take the demi-human form and open the tomb doors for the chosen ones.]],
  str_loading_N48_des_04 = [[
In the vast, chilly ancient house, a grand coffin rests at the hall's center, where flowers never wilt and candles never go out, as if they are the coffin owner's only companions.
Everyone calls the coffin a vampire's ice bed. Still, none are aware that someone once left the town's noise behind and came here, with a soul boiling like hot water, reading, meditating, and looking for the path to Truth alone.]],
  str_loading_N48_des_05 = [[
It's the place where True Order disciples confess and learn. On the night of the Advent of Truth, the Order leaders and family heads jointly lead an important "listening" ceremony.
Disciples are told they must reveal their weak bodies and lie in the coffin with pious hearts. Then, during the family head's chanting, the ancestors of Varaki, and even the Lord of Truth, will descend upon this disciple, speaking revelation through their mouth.]],
  str_loading_c_h_name_laisha1 = "The Lonely Island",
  str_loading_e_h_name_laisha1 = "Land of the Ancient Ruins",
  str_loading_h_desc_laisha1 = "In the distant seas, there lies a lonely island forgotten by the world, surrounded by endless azure and covered with lush dense vegetation. Ancient ruins rest within this pristine verdant cradle, having endured through the ages.",
  str_loading_c_h_name_laisha2 = "Summer Adventure",
  str_loading_e_h_name_laisha2 = "Companions, Together",
  str_loading_h_desc_laisha2 = [[
The island lies silently at the bottom of the sea, along with the evidence of its former glory. Now, a new summer adventure is about to begin.
Companions who stand by your side are the most precious treasures.
In the limited time you have, enjoy this endless adventure with your companions!]],
  str_loading_c_h_name_N5001 = "Harbor City Port",
  str_loading_c_h_name_N5002 = "Aquarium",
  str_loading_c_h_name_N5003 = "Aquarium Fantasy",
  str_loading_e_h_name_N5001 = "The sea breeze gently blows, and migratory birds keep singing.",
  str_loading_e_h_name_N5002 = "The sea on land, a tranquil world.",
  str_loading_e_h_name_N5003 = "The ocean in dream, a world re-recognized.",
  str_loading_h_desc_N5001 = [[
Harbor City, a rare place of tranquility on Astra.
Yet, a sense of calm often precedes upheaval.
Despite the inevitable storms, the city, like the enduring waves, always rebounds.]],
  str_loading_h_desc_N5002 = [[
Fish came from the sea but in the end settled together on land.
With the sound of the conch, they fall into a peaceful dream.
And this harmonious scene becomes a wonderland for visitors.]],
  str_loading_h_desc_N5003 = [[
Have you ever dreamed? In dreams, the ordinary twists into the uncanny.
Like a shadowy, shimmering backroom, there's an eerie familiarity to the unknown.
It's in these twilight realms of the mind that we rediscover the world we thought we knew.]],
  str_loading_21001_name = "Dark Zone Lands",
  str_loading_21001_name_title = "Half Step from Eternal Night",
  str_loading_21001_desc = [[
For Aurorians, entering the Dark Zone is like giving up life itself.
No Lumina supports them here, only shadows that choke all.
But for the Eclipse, it's an ideal hunting ground.
Yet, even so, the fearless forge through the fog, determined to uncover the secrets within.]],
  str_loading_21002_name = "Unexplored Sector 44",
  str_loading_21002_name_title = "Coral Grounds",
  str_loading_21002_desc = [[
A lifeless land overrun by coral.
Time seems frozen here, and light has forsaken it.
Some traces of life can still be found at its borders.
But for those still wandering here, it matters not.
This is a place cursed to repel the light, damning all living beings.]]
}
return config
